  "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $\u2202A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $\u2202A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/4f65a735e53130f633635fdfc8cd6de6c4fa39ed1fb7913ba9679bb07e73a6a0.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-\u2202A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/c76cea9b33420bf6c2e03d8eecb105003ce8b4e619063cbf2b7fccd5bc596cb2.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
